	(text "(check) before freezing:\n- U201 footprint: KiCad QFN-32 5x5 EP 3.45 mm; datasheet EP is 3.5 nom (3.4-3.6). Compare with Nordic's QFN reference layout.\n- D201 part number (leakage < 50 nA at 5 V), L201 part number, R201 value (or delete).\n- GPIO3 for PMIC_INT: match the nPM1304-EK / Zephyr devicetree used in Stage 0b.\n- BUCK1 at 1.8 V -5% = 1.71 V vs the nRF54L15 1.7 V minimum.\n- VSYS abs max 5.5 V: dock supply must stay at 5.0 V; DRV2605L blocked while VBUS is present."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 213.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "050af680-c5f1-4f42-9e4b-6bfe2d581ee9")
	)
	(text "nPM1304 power sheet (step 3). Based on Nordic nPM1304 datasheet, reference circuit 'Configuration 2' (QFN):\none buck, no LDO/load switch, ship-mode exit and NTC used. Draft until the Stage 0b nPM1304-EK tests."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "33d5e37f-70a6-4399-b92c-930ac5c4abae")
	)
	(text "Strapping and connections (from the datasheet):\n- VBUS from dock pad VIN. VBUS abs max 22 V; OVP 5.5 V typ; VBUSPOR 3.9 V. TVS: Vrwm >= 5.5 V, clamp < 22 V.\n- CC1/CC2 to GND: no USB-C; VBUS limit stays at the 100 mA default (enough for 40-55 mA charging).\n- VBUSOUT not used by the SoC but needs its 1 uF decoupling cap.\n- VSET1 = 47k -> BUCK1 starts at 1.8 V (datasheet table: 47k = 1.8 V, max 5% tolerance). VOUT1 = VDD_1V8.\n- BUCK2 unused: VSET2 to GND (off), VOUT2 to VSYS, SW2 open, PVSS2 to GND, no inductor (as in reference config 2).\n- LOADSW1/2 unused: LSIN1, LSOUT1, LSIN2, LSOUT2 to GND (as in reference config 3). LED0-2 open.\n- VDDIO from VOUT1. Unused GPIO0/1/2/4 open: default is input with weak pull-down.\n- PMIC_INT on GPIO3 (any GPIO can be the interrupt; set in devicetree).\n- PVSS1 joins GND through net tie NT201 (one via to the GND layer), as in the reference layout.\n- NTC: 10k 1% B25/50 = 3380 K, one of the three supported types; JEITA defaults match it. Max 100 pF across it.\n- SHPHLD has an internal 50k pull-up. Ship mode exits on SHPHLD low (button to GND) OR VBUS > VBUSPOR,\n  so docking alone wakes the band (still confirm on the EK in Stage 0b). R201 is an optional extra pull-up to VBAT.\n- TWI address 0x6B. I2C pull-ups R203/R204 serve the whole 1.8 V bus (4.7k for 400 kHz).\n- JP201: cut to put the PPK2 in series with the cell; bridge again with solder."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 213.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
